{"schemaVersion":2,"id":"practice-专项-source-a980f519df83","kind":"practice","title":"【未上传】专题十　推测词义（试题word）（可作答题）","year":"专项","region":"资料","variant":"可作答资料","instructions":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"专题十　推测词义"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"— 五年高考—"}]}],"sections":[{"id":"section-legacy","title":"旧卷综合题型","instructions":[],"layout":"flow","groups":[{"id":"group-legacy","instructions":[],"stimulusBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A组　新高考卷题组"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Passage 1(2021新高考Ⅰ,C)　词数 305"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"　　When the explorers first set foot upon the continent of North America, the skies and lands were alive with an astonishing variety of wildlife. Native Americans had taken care of these precious natural resources wisely. Unfortunately, it took the explorers and the settlers who followed only a few decades to decimate a large part of these resources. Millions of waterfowl(水禽) were killed at the hands of market hunters and a handful of overly ambitious sportsmen. Millions of acres of wetlands were dried to feed and house the ever-increasing populations, greatly reducing waterfowl habitat (栖息地)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"In 1934,with the passage of the Migratory Bird Hunting Stamp Act (Act), an increasingly concerned nation took firm action to stop the destruction of migratory(迁徙的)waterfowl and the wetlands so vital to their survival. Under this Act, all waterfowl hunters 16 years of age and over must annually purchase and carry a Federal Duck Stamp. The very first Federal Duck Stamp was designed by J.N. “Ding” Darling, a political cartoonist from Des Moines, Iowa, who at that time was appointed by President Franklin Roosevelt as Director of the Bureau of Biological Survey. Hunters willingly pay the stamp price to ensure the survival of our natural resources."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"About 98 cents of every duck stamp dollar goes directly into the Migratory Bird Conservation Fund to purchase wetlands and wildlife habitat for inclusion into the National Wildlife Refuge System—a fact that ensures this land will be protected and available for all generations to come. Since 1934, better than half a billion dollars has gone into that Fund to purchase more than 5 million acres of habitat. Little wonder the Federal Duck Stamp Program has been called one of the most successful conservation programs ever initiated."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"1.What was a cause of the waterfowl population decline in North America?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A.Loss of wetlands."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"B.Popularity of water sports."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"C.Pollution of rivers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"D.Arrival of other wild animals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"2.What does the underlined word “decimate” mean in the first paragraph?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A.Acquire.　　B.Export."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"C.Destroy.　　D.Distribute."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"3.What is a direct result of the Act passed in 1934?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"A.The stamp price has gone down."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"B.The migratory birds have flown away."}]},{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"C.The hunters have stopped hunting."}]}],"sharedOptions":[],"questions":[{"id":"q-1","displayNumber":1,"sourceQuestionNumber":1,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"What was a cause of the waterfowl population decline in North America?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Loss of wetlands."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Popularity of water sports."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Pollution of rivers."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrival of other wild animals."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["B"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":true,"collapseSpaces":true,"caseSensitive":false}},"explanationBlocks":[],"sourceRefs":[{"sourceDocumentId":"a980f519df8302948e419fc44aa283f314836e006b05fad7a98eaf7892f3fd6c","relativePath":"题型/【未上传】专题十　推测词义（试题word）.docx","sha256":"a980f519df8302948e419fc44aa283f314836e006b05fad7a98eaf7892f3fd6c","locator":{},"extractionMethod":"docx-xml","confidence":0.96}],"reviewStatus":"approved","dedupeSignature":{"questionContentFingerprint":"eb05475353488ef71f5b942fc030cac713234393791ec5bfa45809cdfbafc526","answerVariantFingerprint":"ef68c7224a85b4e9f0fbdb0f28f12d220aafab811edcdac38404d4de9272e4ff"}},{"id":"q-2","displayNumber":2,"sourceQuestionNumber":2,"type":"single_choice","promptBlocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"What does the underlined word “decimate” mean in the first paragraph?"}]}],"placement":{"kind":"standalone"},"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Acquire."}]}]},{"id":"B","label":"B","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Export."}]}]},{"id":"C","label":"C","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Destroy."}]}]},{"id":"D","label":"D","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","runs":[{"type":"text","text":"Distribute."}]}]}],"blanks":[],"answerSpec":{"availability":"answered","gradingMode":"auto","kind":"choice","acceptedAnswers":["D"],"normalization":{"unicodeNfkc":true,"trim":tru